# Rule 3: recursion only folds.  A function that calls itself at the same
# instantiation recurses on a value, which nothing the compiler sees bounds.
# Recursion over a type's structure passes by construction: cata on a
# composite calls cata on its parts, each a different specialisation, and
# the compiler's instantiation limit bounds the rest.  Instantiations are
# where a template's self-calls resolve, hence the traversal.  Blind spots:
# mutual recursion (needs a call graph), and a template never instantiated
# in the file being checked.
# The function is identified by its body, which every redeclaration shares,
# so an out-of-line member definition is the same function as its in-class
# declaration.  Constructors recurse by construction expressions, matched
# apart.  Calls in unevaluated operands (sizeof, decltype, noexcept) are not
# recursion; a self-reference inside a requires-expression is (clang-query
# has no matcher for one) a known false positive.
set traversal AsIs
match callExpr(hasAncestor(functionDecl(hasBody(compoundStmt().bind("body")))), callee(functionDecl(hasBody(compoundStmt(equalsBoundNode("body"))))), unless(hasAncestor(unaryExprOrTypeTraitExpr())), unless(hasAncestor(cxxNoexceptExpr())), unless(hasAncestor(typeLoc(loc(decltypeType())))), isExpansionInMainFile(), hasAncestor(scope))
match cxxConstructExpr(hasAncestor(cxxConstructorDecl(hasBody(compoundStmt().bind("body")))), hasDeclaration(cxxConstructorDecl(hasBody(compoundStmt(equalsBoundNode("body"))))), unless(hasAncestor(unaryExprOrTypeTraitExpr())), unless(hasAncestor(cxxNoexceptExpr())), unless(hasAncestor(typeLoc(loc(decltypeType())))), isExpansionInMainFile(), hasAncestor(scope))
